            <span class="install-cmd" id="install-cmd">npm install -g metalmind</span>
            <button type="button" class="install-copy" data-copy-target="install-cmd" aria-label="Copy install command">copy</button>
          </div>
          <div class="install-note">
            <a class="install-chip install-chip-live" href={`https://www.npmjs.com/package/metalmind/v/${version}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Live on npm · v{version}</a>
            <span>Then run <code>metalmind init</code>.</span>
          </div>
          <p class="install-scope">
            <strong>MIT · local-only · no cloud · no accounts · reversible in one command.</strong>
            Claude Code today; Cursor / Codex / Copilot / Gemini on the roadmap.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Nikitzu/metalmind">view on GitHub →</a>
          <a class="btn-stars" href="https://github.com/Nikitzu/metalmind" aria-label="GitHub stars">
            <img src="https://img.shields.io/github/stars/Nikitzu/metalmind?style=flat-square&color=d4a14a&labelColor=10141b&label=stars" alt="GitHub stars" />
          </a>
        </div>

        <p class="hero-flavor-note scadrial-only">
          <em>Scadrial flavor:</em> commands are named after Mistborn Era&nbsp;1 metals —
          <strong>copper</strong> stores memory, <strong>bronze</strong> reads the code graph,
          <strong>iron/steel</strong> navigate and rename symbols. Prefer plain verbs?
          Switch to <label for="flavor-classic" class="inline-toggle">Classic</label> in the top-right
          — every themed command has a plain alias (<code>tap copper</code> ↔ <code>recall</code>,
          <code>burn bronze</code> ↔ <code>graph</code>, etc.) and both always work at the CLI.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="proof-band container-wide" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
